<title>INDIA: Indian soybean, oil down, meal up.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean, oil down, meal up.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soybean prices were bearish on poor demand from processing plants on Thursday, dealers said.</p>
<p>Prices were down by 200 rupees per tonne in central Indian markets. All markets will be closed on Friday to mark India's 50th anniversary of independence, as well as on Monday for the Hindu religious festival 'Raksha Bandhan'.</p>
<p>Soyoil prices were also bearish. Soyoil solvent was down by 200 rupees and soyoil refined was down by 100 rupees per tonne as demand was poor. Business volume was dull and the undertone was easy.</p>
<p>Soymeal and rapeseed extraction prices were slightly up on tight supply. Soymeal yellow was $264-265 per tonne FAS (free alongside ship) at west Indian ports for export. Rapeseed extraction was $94-95 per tonne FAS in bulk for export and was 3,275-3,300 rupees per tonne in FOR (free on rail) condition.</p>
